# KOR: Eternal Frontier

This repository's active game is the standalone .NET/Gondwana implementation in `GondwanaGame/`. The Unity project and editor-bound assets are legacy prototype material and are not required for the actual game build or development workflow.

## Canonical app

The real application is the C#/.NET 8 project in `GondwanaGame/` with its own SDL3 + SkiaSharp runtime and deterministic scenario checks.

## Quick start (Linux)

Prerequisites:
- .NET 8 SDK
- SDL3 runtime (`libSDL3.so.0`)
- a desktop session for graphical play

From the repository root:

```bash
./build-linux.sh
./launch-kor.sh
```

Development / verification commands:

```bash
cd GondwanaGame
dotnet build GondwanaGame.csproj --configuration Release
dotnet run --project GondwanaGame.csproj --configuration Release -- --self-test
SDL_VIDEODRIVER=offscreen dotnet run --project GondwanaGame.csproj --configuration Release -- --smoke-test
dotnet publish GondwanaGame.csproj --configuration Release --runtime linux-x64 --self-contained true --output GondwanaGame/artifacts/linux-x64
```

## Legacy status

The Unity files in `Assets/`, `ProjectSettings/`, and related root directories are retained only for historical reference. They are not part of the active build, launch, or test path.

## Notes

- The canonical build and self-test path is `GondwanaGame/`.
- The root wrapper scripts target the same canonical project so the repository has a single active application entry point.
- Builds and tests are validated against the Linux target, not against the Unity editor workflow.
